  "method": "The residual at the published fit's own anchors, diffused over the mesh. Anchors are recomputed by the fit's rule; only the camera is re-solved, against this machine's detection of the same portraits, every digest matching. The smoothness is chosen per subject: the tightest rung of a fixed ladder that turns no triangle over.",
  "limits": [
    "A weak perspective fit of one portrait observes no depth, so the delta lies in the image plane and has no component along the view axis",
    "An anchor outside every triangle, and one whose residual stands three interquartile ranges beyond the rest, is dropped rather than allowed to pull geometry after it",
    "Rows below a hundredth of a millimetre are dropped: below the mesh's own numerical noise and below anything a render resolves",
    "The residual reduction is not the same for everyone. Where a portrait was taken at an angle the camera cannot take out, the residual is pose rather than shape, and forcing it into vertices folds the mesh; those subjects take the smoothest field and gain least"
  ]
